Sure, here are a few Python practice problems you can try:

    Write a function that takes a list of numbers as input and returns a new list with only the even numbers.

    Write a function that takes a string as input and returns a new string that is the reverse of the input.

    Write a function that takes two lists as input and returns a new list that contains only the elements that are common between the lists (without duplicates). Make sure your program works on two lists of different sizes.

    Write a function that checks whether a passed string is a palindrome or not.

    Write a function that takes an integer n and prints the Fibonacci series up to n.

Remember, the goal is not just to solve these problems, but to practice thinking algorithmically and coding in Python. Good luck!
